== the ward knows your name now
tier: inner
threshold: title:local councillor
step: 3
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-90
times: per new local councillor: once, about five months after taking the title, near the end of the threshold season; about 1 life in 100 (catalogue share)
holds: local councillor
stakes: .8
tone: joy
life: public life, friends
horizon: months
roles: friend, colleague, partner
earth: five months in, people stop you in the shop, ask after the drain and the bus stop, and old friends ring for favours
tribal: five moons in, the families greet you by name at the water, ask after their quarrels, and old friends want your voice
magic: five months in, the lane's children call you by your title, the baker will not take your coin, and old friends want a quiet word
requires: in the threshold season of local councillor, within the first six months after taking the title: step 3, near the end of the six months, as the new life settles
likelier: a councillor who lives in the ward; a few cases settled; a local paper or a ward newsletter that carries the name
rarer: a councillor who lives outside the ward; a council in open crisis
scene: Five months in, {N} cannot buy milk without being stopped twice: once about a pothole, once to be thanked for a bus stop. {friend} jokes that {N} has become a landmark, and an old school friend has rung twice about "a quiet word" on a licence.
scene W: The surgery runs every second Saturday, the minutes go out on time, and residents have started to say the ward is properly looked after.
scene U: {N} can now read a planning report in twenty minutes and find the paragraph the officers hoped nobody would notice.
scene B: The old school friend's quiet word is the third such request this month. {N} is starting to see what a councillor's name is worth.
scene R: The fizz of the first night has gone. Some evenings {N} misses being an ordinary person in the pub.
scene G: {N} knows the streets in a new way now: who is ill, who has moved, which corner floods. The ward feels like a wide family, with all that brings.
scene tribal: Five moons in, the families greet {N} by name at the water, and an old friend sits down at {Ns} fire wanting {Ns} voice in a quarrel of their own.
scene magic: Five months in, the lane's children call {N} by title, the baker will not take {Ns} coin, and an old friend wants a quiet word about a guild licence.
- W | keep the fortnightly surgery going, rain or shine, even when nobody comes | habit | v: conformity, benevolence | tribal: keep your hearth open on the set day each moon, even when nobody comes | magic: keep the petition day going every fortnight, even when nobody comes | chance: 85
- U | send the ward a short monthly report on what you did and did not manage | v: universalism, achievement | tribal: tell the families at each new moon what you managed at the fire, and what you did not | magic: post a short monthly account on the ward's notice board of what you did and did not manage | chance: 92
- B | keep a quiet list of every favour you do, and of who owes you | habit | v: power | self_control: + | tribal: keep count in your head of every favour you do, and of who owes you | chance: 95
- R | spend a Saturday night in the pub as yourself, councillor or not | habit | v: hedonism, self-direction | tribal: spend a night at the dancing as yourself, a voice at the fire or not | magic: spend a night at the tavern as yourself, councillor or not | chance: 88
- G | walk the whole ward on Sundays, stopping for anyone who wants to talk | v: benevolence, tradition | tribal: walk round every hearth of the camp, stopping for anyone who wants to talk | magic: walk the whole ward on market days, stopping for anyone who wants to talk | chance: 75
- W>G | start a residents' forum that meets in the library every month | v: benevolence, conformity | tribal: call the families of your hearths together at every new moon to talk things through | magic: start a monthly meeting of the lane's households in the old reading room | chance: 65
- U>W | read the code of conduct again, and declare every interest, even the small ones | v: conformity, security | tribal: ask the elders which gifts a voice at the fire may take, and refuse the rest | magic: read the council's oath again, and declare every interest, even the small ones | chance: 96
- B>U | trade your vote on a small item for a place on the scrutiny committee | door | v: achievement, power | tribal: trade your voice on a small matter for a place among the elders who weigh the stores | magic: trade your vote on a small item for a seat on the council's audit bench | chance: 78
- R>B | tell the old friend no to their face, loudly enough for the whole pub to hear | v: power, self-direction | grants: a name for straight talk | tribal: refuse the old friend's favour at the fire, loudly enough for the whole band to hear | magic: refuse the old friend's favour in the tavern, loudly enough for the whole room to hear | chance: 84
- G>R | plant up the ugly corner by the bus stop with the neighbours, for fun | body: light | v: hedonism, benevolence | mark: made a friend | tribal: clear and plant the trampled ground by the water with the families, for the joy of it | magic: plant up the bare corner by the well with the neighbours, for the fun of it | chance: 90
works: The ward has got used to {N}, and {N} has got used to being the ward's.
works: {friend} says {N} is still the same person, just busier, and means it kindly.
fails: The favours, the calls and the stops in the street wear {N} thin by the end of the month.
fails: One unanswered request turns into a story about {N} that goes round every street.

# ================================================================ mayor (ages 21-95)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 76. step 1 (cycle s1)

== the chain of office
tier: inner
threshold: title:mayor
step: 1
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 21-95
times: per new mayor: once, in the first weeks after taking the title; about 1 life in 500 (catalogue share; estimate)
holds: mayor
stakes: .8
tone: joy
life: public life, work
horizon: week
roles: colleague, elder, boss
earth: the chain goes round your neck in the council chamber, and on Monday the office, the staff and the diary are yours
tribal: the band gathers at dawn to see the head of the camp take up the old staff, and the first question is where to camp next
magic: the burgomaster's chain, seal and keys are handed over in the town hall, and the clerks wait for your first order
requires: in the threshold season of mayor, within the first six months after taking the title (opened by 'the town needs a mayor', a direct election or any other way in): step 1, the first weeks in office
likelier: a contested choice won; a town with an old mayoral office and its ceremonies; a mayor new to the town hall's staff
rarer: a deputy who steps up after years in the office; a small place where the mayor's post is one evening a week
scene: The chain is heavier than it looks. After the ceremony {N} is shown the mayor's office: a desk, a window over the square, a diary already full for six weeks and a secretary who has served four mayors.
scene W: {N} reads the declaration of office aloud in the chamber without a slip, and means every word of it.
scene U: {N} asks for the town's accounts, the list of contracts and the staff chart before the first meeting, and reads them all weekend.
scene B: The diary is full of other people's priorities. {N} looks at it and starts deciding which of them to cancel.
scene R: {N} wants to walk straight out of the chamber, still in the chain, into the market, and shake every hand there.
scene G: In the corridor hang portraits of every mayor for a hundred and fifty years. {N} stops at each one on the way to the office.
scene tribal: At dawn the band gathers as the old staff of the camp passes into {Ns} hands, and the first question is already waiting: where to camp when the river rises.
scene magic: In the town hall the old burgomaster lifts the chain over {Ns} head and hands over the seal and the keys, and the clerks wait, quills ready, for the first order.
- W | keep the diary as the office set it for the first month, and learn from it | v: conformity, security | tribal: keep to the old order of the head's days for the first moon, and learn from it | magic: keep the burgomaster's book of days as the clerks set it for the first month | chance: 94
- U | spend the first weekend reading the town's accounts and every big contract | v: achievement | mark: learned a skill | tribal: walk the whole camp counting the stores, the hides and the tools | magic: spend the first days reading the town's ledgers and every guild charter | chance: 95
- B | cancel half the diary, and fill it with meetings that serve your own plan | v: power, self-direction | tribal: set aside the elders' plans for the season, and put your own in their place | magic: strike half the appointments from the book, and fill it with your own | chance: 89
- R | walk out into the market in the chain, and shake every hand you can | body: light | v: stimulation, hedonism | tribal: go round every hearth at once with the staff in your hand | chance: 96
- G | ask the secretary who served four mayors what each of them got wrong | v: tradition, achievement | mark: made a friend | tribal: ask the oldest woman of the camp what each head before you got wrong | magic: ask the old clerk who served four burgomasters what each of them got wrong | chance: 80
- W>U | get the town clerk's briefing on the law of the office before signing anything | v: conformity, achievement | tribal: ask the elders for the old rules of the head of the camp before deciding anything | magic: get the town clerk's briefing on the law of the office before setting your seal to anything | chance: 96
- U>B | find out which officers really run the town hall, and win them over first | v: power, achievement | tribal: find out which families really decide things in the camp, and win them first | magic: find out which clerks really run the town hall, and win them over first | chance: 79
- B>R | get a local firm to pay for a party in the square on the first Saturday | v: hedonism, power | tribal: get the richest family to give a feast for the whole camp | magic: get a merchant house to pay for a feast in the square on the first market day | chance: 86
- R>G | open the mayor's parlour to anyone who wants to see it, every Friday | v: benevolence, stimulation | tribal: let anyone who wants to sit at the head's fire, every evening | magic: open the burgomaster's hall to anyone who wants to see it, every market day | chance: 92
- G>W | visit every care home and school in town in the first month, as old mayors did | v: tradition, benevolence | tribal: visit every old one and every mother of small children in the camp, as the old heads did | magic: visit every almshouse and school in town in the first month, as the old burgomasters did | chance: 78
works: By the end of the first week the post feels less like a ceremony and more like work.
works: The town takes to {N} in the chain, and the first days go better than anyone feared.
fails: The first week goes on ceremonies and handshakes, and nothing {N} came to do has started.
fails: An early decision upsets the old guard, and the corridors are cool toward {N} for weeks.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 77. step 2 (cycle s2)

== the day job or the town
tier: inner
threshold: title:mayor
step: 2
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 21-95
times: per new mayor: once, about ten weeks into the threshold season, for about half of new mayors (the season's middle step brings this moment or 'the kind of mayor you will be'); about 1 life in 500 is a mayor (catalogue share; estimate), so about 1 in 1,000 meet it
holds: mayor
stakes: .8
tone: trouble
life: public life, work, family
horizon: months
roles: boss, partner, colleague
earth: ten weeks in, the town needs a mayor every day of the week, and your employer needs you back on Monday
tribal: two moons in, the hunt leaves at the new moon, and the camp cannot be left without its head; you cannot do both
magic: ten weeks in, your workshop and your guild's work wait, while the town needs its burgomaster every hour the bells ring
