scene W: {N} promised the town a mayor who would be there, and promised {boss} at work a full week. Both cannot be true.
scene U: {N} works it out on paper: hours, pay, pension, the allowance, and what a part-time mayor of a town this size can and cannot do.
scene B: The town's business brings more contacts in a week than the day job did in ten years. {N} wonders which of the two is really the career now.
scene R: {N} loves the work at the town hall and dreads Mondays at the old job. It has never been so plain.
scene G: The day job pays for the house and the family's peace of mind, and {partner} is afraid of what happens if the town throws {N} out at the next election.
scene tribal: The hunt leaves at the new moon, and {Ns} spear has always gone with it. But a camp left without its head while the river rises is a camp in danger.
scene magic: {Ns} workbench at the guild has been cold for weeks, the masters are asking questions, and the town needs its burgomaster every hour the bells ring.
