- R>G | bring your campaign volunteers on a tour of the building | v: benevolence | mark: kept your word | tribal: bring the young ones who walked the hearths in your name to see the gathering | magic: bring your banner-bearers on a tour of the Assembly's halls | chance: 96
- G>W | open an office in the old place on the high street, open every Friday | v: benevolence, tradition | tribal: keep a fire burning at home for the families each time you return from the gathering | magic: open your petition room in the old place on the high street, every market day | chance: 72
works: By the end of the first week {N} can find the chamber, the library and the way home without asking.
works: An old member stops {N} in a corridor, says {N} will do well here, and seems to mean it.
fails: The first week passes in a blur of corridors, forms and waiting, and {N} is not sure what {N} did.
