scene: Ten weeks in, {Ns} name is down for the maiden speech. By custom it praises the constituency, avoids a fight and is heard in silence. {N} has eight drafts, and {mentor} has read three of them.
scene W: The custom is clear: praise the member who came before, describe the constituency, avoid controversy. {N} finds a dignity in it.
scene U: {N} wants a speech that is accurate in every figure and says one thing nobody in the house has quite said before.
scene B: Speeches like this are clipped, quoted and remembered when the whips draw up their lists. {N} writes with that in mind.
scene R: {N} wants to tear up the custom and say what the people back home are really angry about, in their own words.
scene G: {N} wants the house to hear the place: the river, the closed pit, the old market, the accent.
scene tribal: For the first time {N} will speak before all the clans. By custom a first speaker tells of the band that sent them and starts no quarrel, and every speaker listens.
scene magic: {Ns} first oration in the Assembly is set for the morning bell. By custom it praises the city that sent its member, and the whole Assembly will be listening.
