== the brief you did not ask for
tier: inner
threshold: title:minister
step: 2
stages: adult mature elder
age: 21-95
times: per new minister: once, about ten weeks into the threshold season, for about half of new ministers (the season's middle step brings this moment or 'the decision that will carry your name'); about 1 life in 30,000 is a minister (catalogue share; estimate), so about 1 in 60,000 meet it
holds: minister
stakes: .8
tone: trouble
life: public life, work
horizon: months
roles: boss, colleague, partner
earth: ten weeks in, the brief you were given is not the one you wanted, the subject is one you knew nothing about, and the leader expects results
tribal: two moons in, the chief gave you the peace with the river clans when you know only the hunt, and the chief wants the peace kept
magic: ten weeks in, the throne gave you the Wardenship of the Roads when your heart was in the Treasury, and the throne expects the roads mended
requires: in the threshold season of minister, within the first six months after taking the title: step 2, some weeks into the post, when it is clear the post is not the one the person hoped for
likelier: a minister given a post outside their own field; a leader who uses posts to reward and to punish; a junior post
rarer: a minister given the post they asked for; a specialist appointed for their expertise
scene: Ten weeks in, {N} is still the minister for a subject {N} knew nothing about on the day of the phone call. {N} wanted another post; {boss} gave this one and wants results by the summer. In the safe is a report on the department's failures that the last minister kept from the house.
scene W: Ministers serve where they are sent. {N} has said it to {partner} several times this month, as if to be convinced.
scene U: A whole new field to master: its law, its history, its numbers, its experts. Part of {N} is delighted.
scene B: A post nobody wanted is a post nobody watches. {N} sees room in that.
scene R: {N} feels sidelined and a little humiliated, and the buried report makes {N} angrier every time {N} reads it.
scene G: The officials have worked in this field for thirty years. {N} is the eleventh minister they have had in that time.
scene tribal: The chief gave {N} the peace with the river clans, when {N} knows only the hunt. The old hands whisper about a promise the last keeper made to the river clans and never kept.
scene magic: The throne gave {N} the Wardenship of the Roads, when {Ns} heart was in the Treasury. In a locked chest lies the report on the roads that the last Warden kept from the Assembly.
- W | serve where the leader put you, and do the post properly, without complaint | v: conformity | tribal: keep the duty the chief gave you, and keep it well, without complaint | magic: serve where the throne put you, and do the office properly, without complaint | chance: 95
- U | read yourself into the subject: its law, its history and its experts, every evening | habit | v: achievement, self-direction | grants: drafting policy | tribal: learn everything about the duty from those who know it, every evening | magic: read yourself into the office: its law, its history and its scholars, every evening | chance: 72
- B | use the quiet post to build allies in cabinet for the post you really want | v: power, achievement | grants: allies in the party | tribal: use the quiet duty to win friends among the chief's speakers for the duty you want | magic: use the quiet office to win friends among the councillors for the seat you want | chance: 78
- R | leak the buried report to a journalist friend, so the public knows | v: stimulation, universalism | mark: hid a wrong | closed: approval: leaking a confidential report; backfire: a leak inquiry traces it, and the leader asks for the minister's resignation | self_control: - | tribal: tell a singer what the last keeper hid, so every fire hears of it | magic: slip the buried report to a broadsheet writer, so the whole city knows | chance: 92
- G | ask the oldest officials what was tried in this field before, and what came of it | v: tradition, achievement | tribal: ask the oldest hands what was tried before, and what came of it | magic: ask the oldest clerks what was tried before, and what came of it | chance: 75
- W>B | ask formally for a move at the next reshuffle, and do this post well meanwhile | v: achievement, conformity | tribal: ask the chief, by custom, for another duty at the next gathering, and keep this one well | magic: petition the throne for another office, and do this one well meanwhile | chance: 35
- U>R | find the bold reform this field has needed for years, and argue it on the evidence | v: self-direction, universalism | tribal: find the bold change the duty has needed for years, and argue it from what is known | chance: 40
- B>G | keep the post safe: avoid every risk, guard the budget, and wait | v: security | self_control: + | tribal: keep the duty safe: risk nothing, guard its share, and wait | magic: keep the office safe: risk nothing, guard its coffer, and wait | chance: 92
- R>W | publish the buried report yourself, openly, and take the blame for what it shows | v: universalism | mark: owned up | tribal: tell the whole gathering what the last keeper hid, openly, and carry the blame | magic: publish the buried report yourself, under your own seal, and take the blame | chance: 65
- G>U | spend a week out in the field with the people the department serves, and listen | door | v: benevolence, universalism | tribal: spend a moon among the people the duty touches, and listen | magic: spend a week among the people the office serves, and listen | chance: 78
works: By the end of the month {N} knows the subject well enough to hold a room on it.
works: {boss} says in front of the others that {N} has taken a hard post and made something of it.
fails: Every week shows how little {N} knows, and the officials have started to manage {N} rather than serve.
fails: {Ns} frustration shows, and word reaches the leader that {N} is sulking.

