== the decision that will carry your name
tier: inner
threshold: title:minister
step: 2
transform: yes
stages: adult mature elder
age: 21-95
times: per new minister: once in the threshold season, for about half of new ministers (the season's middle step brings this moment or 'the brief you did not ask for'); about 1 life in 30,000 is a minister (catalogue share; estimate), so about 1 in 60,000 meet it
holds: minister
stakes: .8
tone: mixed
life: public life, meaning
horizon: years
roles: boss, colleague, rival
earth: ten weeks in, one decision in the department will outlast you, and how you make it will decide what kind of minister you are
tribal: two moons in, the duty the chief gave you holds one choice the clans will remember for a generation, and it is yours to make
magic: ten weeks in, one decree under your seal will outlast your office, and the court is waiting to see what kind of councillor you are
requires: in the threshold season of minister, within the first six months after taking the title: step 2, the season's transforming chance, when the department's big decision of the term reaches the minister's desk
likelier: a department with a reform long waited for; a leader who leaves the minister room to choose; a full parliament still ahead
rarer: a caretaker government near its end; a junior post with no decisions of its own
scene: Ten weeks in, one decision in the department will outlast {N}: a reform the field has waited years for, a rule that will bear the minister's name. {N} can make it in many ways, and each would make a different kind of minister.
scene W: {N} wants a reform built to last: consulted on, written into law, defended in the house and fair to everyone it touches.
scene U: {N} has the evidence, the pilots and the models. It could be the best-designed reform in a generation, if {N} has the patience.
scene B: A reform that bears {Ns} name is power: in cabinet, in the party, in the next leadership race. {N} means to make it count.
scene R: The people this field has failed are angry, and {N} is angry with them. This is the chance to do something big, now.
scene G: Some things in this field have worked for a hundred years. {N} is wary of breaking what holds, even while mending what does not.
scene tribal: One choice in the duty the chief gave {N} will be remembered for a generation: how the hunting grounds are shared, or which clans the band trades with. It is {Ns} to make.
scene magic: One decree under {Ns} seal will outlast the office, and the whole court is waiting to see what kind of councillor of the Crown {N} means to be.
