- G | guard the country's land, towns and ways, and change only what must change | identity | v: tradition | tribal: guard the clans' lands, hunts and ways, and change only what must change | magic: ask the oldest oracle of the realm what the land needs, and guard that above all | chance: 72
- W>R | write a charter of the people's rights, and bind the government to it | identity | binds | v: universalism, self-direction | tribal: set down before all the clans what no chief may take from a family, and bind yourself to it | magic: draft a charter of the people's rights, and bind the Chancellery to it by oath | chance: 30
- U>G | plan a generation's renewal of the land, the rivers and the forgotten towns | identity | binds | v: universalism, tradition | tribal: plan, for a generation, how the clans can share the valley's land and rivers | magic: plan a generation's renewal of the land, the rivers and the forgotten towns of the realm | chance: 58
- B>W | build a coalition so broad that nobody can bring the government down | identity | binds | v: power | grants: coalition building | tribal: bind so many clans to your fire that nobody can bring you down | magic: bind so many factions and Orders to you that nobody can bring the Chancellery down | chance: 35
- R>U | try bold reforms quickly, and keep only what works | identity | v: stimulation, achievement | tribal: try new ways quickly, and keep only what works | chance: 40
- G>B | make the country strong on its own: its food, its energy and its towns | identity | binds | v: power, tradition | tribal: make the clans strong on their own: their food, their stores and their camps | magic: make the realm strong on its own: its grain, its mines and its towns | chance: 65
works: The answer, once given, holds: ministers, officials and the country start to know what the government is for.
works: Months later people who never backed {N} can still say what {N} stands for, and say it fairly.
fails: The answer is lost in the next week's crises, and the government drifts from day to day.
fails: What {N} says the government is for and what it does start to drift apart, and the other side notices first.

